{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "2026-10-13T05:53:41.831316+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-13T05:53:45.513207+00:00", "id": 23333353, "conceptrecid": "23333352", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23333353", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23333352", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23333353", "metadata": {"title": "Ambient Dependence of Extremal-Exchangeable Independence", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23333353", "publication_date": "2026-10-12", "description": "<p>We give explicit counterexamples answering the ambient-algebra question in Liebscher's unrestricted extremal-exchangeable free-product definition of independence. A state-preserving unital inclusion of the four-point algebra into M4(C) makes two distinct proper coordinate subalgebras with scalar intersection dependent downstairs and independent upstairs. Positivity forces every downstairs witness to be a nontrivial character mixture; a pure folding witness works upstairs.</p><p>The three-page research note separately proves algebraic non-lifting via C[x] contained in C[x,x^-1], and explains extreme-state lifting for equivariant unital C*-inclusions. Pure folding and the extremality framework are established prior mathematics and are credited. The claim uses all-exchangeable extremality and unital algebraic/universal C*-free products, without a fixed-marginal convex slice, faithfulness, trace, or normal W*-requirement. The deposit includes source, exact rational verification, independent mathematical reviews and a bounded primary-source priority audit. Historical-first priority and a still-open-in-2026 assertion are not made.</p><p>AI tools were used extensively in development, writing, reproduction and adversarial verification. This is an unrefereed preprint with internal AI adversarial reviews; it has not received human peer review.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kriebel, Alec", "affiliation": "Independent researcher", "orcid": "0009-0001-9320-500X"}], "keywords": ["exchangeability", "quantum in